---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy & Zero-Upload Guarantee | QuadletGen"
	description="Read QuadletGen's privacy policy: 100% browser-local zero-upload processing for docker-compose.yml files and secrets, anonymized GA4 event policy, and GDPR/CCPA rights."
	canonicalPath="/privacy/"
	showComparison={false}
>
	<article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14 lg:px-8">
		<header class="border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
			<p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400">
				Last Updated: November 12, 2026
			</p>
			<h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
				Privacy Policy and Zero-Upload Data Guarantee
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300 sm:text-base">
				QuadletGen (<code class="text-cyan-300">quadletgen.com</code>) is engineered so your container manifests, private image names, host mount paths, and environment secrets never leave your device.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300 sm:text-base">
			<section class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					1. Zero-upload guarantee for docker-compose.yml files and environment secrets
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					Every conversion step on QuadletGen runs locally inside your web browser's volatile RAM. When you paste a <code class="text-emerald-300">docker-compose.yml</code> manifest, type a <code class="text-emerald-300">docker run</code> or <code class="text-emerald-300">podman run</code> command, select a local <code class="text-emerald-300">.yml</code>, <code class="text-emerald-300">.yaml</code>, or <code class="text-emerald-300">.txt</code> file, extract database passwords into a <code class="text-emerald-300">.env</code> unit, or download a <code class="text-emerald-300">.zip</code> archive, zero bytes of your configuration are uploaded to any server.
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-300">
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">No backend conversion API.</strong> QuadletGen is deployed as pure static HTML, CSS, and client-side JavaScript assets with no database and no form submission endpoints.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">No secret harvesting.</strong> Environment variables, API tokens, TLS paths, container image URLs, and filenames stay strictly inside your browser tab memory and are discarded as soon as you close or refresh the page.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Independently verifiable.</strong> Open your browser DevTools Network inspector while pasting manifests or clicking Download .zip Bundle to confirm zero outbound payload requests carry your input.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					2. Static edge delivery and security logs
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					QuadletGen is served globally over HTTPS through Cloudflare Workers Static Assets. Like any website on the public internet, Cloudflare processes standard HTTP transport metadata (requesting IP address, TLS cipher metadata, User-Agent header, HTTP status code, and requested static URL path) transiently at the network edge for TLS termination, caching, and automated DDoS or abuse mitigation. QuadletGen does not maintain user accounts, login sessions, or application-level access logs linking IP addresses to workbench activity.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					3. Anonymized Google Analytics 4 (GA4) event policy
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					When production measurement is configured on <code class="text-cyan-300">quadletgen.com</code>, we use Google Analytics 4 solely to understand aggregate page traffic and high-level workbench usability, such as which preset routes are visited and whether operators export output via clipboard copy or ZIP download (<code class="text-cyan-300">quadlet_export</code>).
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-300">
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Strict payload scrubbing.</strong> Analytics events carry only coarse action labels (for example <code class="text-cyan-300">copy</code> or <code class="text-cyan-300">zip</code>) and preset route paths. Event parameters never contain YAML text, CLI arguments, stack names, secret keys, or uploaded filenames.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">IP anonymization and ad-signal suppression.</strong> GA4 initialization enforces IP anonymization (<code class="text-cyan-300">anonymize_ip: true</code>) and disables Google Signals and advertising personalization features.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Blocker friendly.</strong> If you use uBlock Origin, Brave Shields, Firefox Enhanced Tracking Protection, Privacy Badger, or the official Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on, all Quadlet conversion and ZIP packaging features continue working identically with zero warnings or degraded functionality.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					4. Cookies and outbound third-party links
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					QuadletGen sets zero authentication or preference cookies of its own. When GA4 loads on the production domain without a content blocker, Google Analytics sets first-party measurement cookies (<code class="text-cyan-300">_ga</code>) to distinguish aggregate repeat visits from single-page bounces. You can clear or block cookies in your browser settings at any time.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3">
					Pages on QuadletGen may link to upstream Podman documentation or clearly disclosed Linux VPS providers (marked <code class="text-cyan-300">rel="sponsored noopener"</code> where commercial). Clicking an external link navigates you to that third party's domain under its own privacy notice.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					5. GDPR (EEA/UK) and CCPA/CPRA (California) privacy rights
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					Depending on where you live, including the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, Switzerland, or California, you have statutory rights regarding personal data:
				</p>
				<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-300">
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Right to know, access, and delete.</strong> Because QuadletGen never collects names, email addresses (unless you email us directly), user accounts, or uploaded container files, we hold no personal profile associated with your browser session. If you email us, you may request access to or deletion of your correspondence at any time.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">No sale or cross-context behavioral sharing.</strong> QuadletGen does not sell, rent, or trade personal information as defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), nor do we share personal data for cross-context behavioral advertising.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="font-semibold text-white">Right to object or restrict analytics.</strong> EEA and UK visitors may block analytics scripts via browser privacy controls or contact us with questions regarding our legitimate-interest safeguards and data minimization architecture.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8">
				<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white sm:text-xl">
					6. Contact for privacy inquiries
				</h2>
				<p class="mt-3">
					For privacy questions, GDPR or CCPA/CPRA requests, or security disclosures, contact <a href="mailto:hello@quadletgen.com" class="font-mono font-medium text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan-200">hello@quadletgen.com</a>. Also review our <a href="/about/" class="font-medium text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan-200">About page</a> and <a href="/terms/" class="font-medium text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-cyan-200">Terms of Service</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
